-- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------
  Title       Yie Ar Kung-Fu (128K)
  Publisher   Imagine, 1985
  Version     1.0

-- YOU NEED ------------------------------------------------------------------
  Your own copy of the original game, saved beside this patch:

  File        Yie Ar Kung-Fu (1985)(Imagine Software)[128K].z80
  MD5         954472db58451ab0183075154cd70169

  The patch carries none of the game's code. It only works with that exact
  dump, under that name or any other: anything else is refused, with a
  message naming the file it wants.

-- WHAT IT DOES --------------------------------------------------------------
  Moving figures become Next hardware sprites, so they keep their own colours
  and no longer take on the scenery's (colour clash). Game logic is unchanged.

  Colours     Default (the game's own) plus: Enhanced, chosen on the menu, off
              by default.
  Enhanced    Oolong and all eleven opponents in the colours of Konami's 1985
              arcade game: clothes, skin, hair and weapons, in flat colours
              with the game's black lines kept and no white edge. Off by
              default. A painted set, colourist not named.

  Changes     1.0: the fighters as Next sprites (the colour clash fix),
              Enhanced colours, two checked cheats and the loading screen
              while patching

  Note        Keys: Space at the title or the scores, then 1 for one player.
              In a fight A and D move, hold S with a direction to attack, and
              Space switches between punches and kicks. Oolong and his
              opponents, the thrown stars and the chain are Next sprites over
              the figures the game still draws: black lines, bodies in the
              ground's colour as in the original (cyan on the lawn, yellow in
              the courtyard), and the same look wherever they move instead of
              the colours of the cells they cross; the hit spark no longer
              colours its cell. At Feedle the waiting fighters stay hidden in
              the black caves. Known issues: the pace has not been compared
              with the original on a Next. Missing: a real Next run.

-- MENU ----------------------------------------------------------------------
   1  Infinite energy
   2  Infinite lives

  Cheats are the archive's POKEs for this release, each checked against the
  code; dropped: seven entries that hit reloadable opponent data, change a
  CALL or JP target, or remove a real extra-life award.

